{"id":34971306841,"name":"Test","node_id":"WFR_kwLOA_1uaM8AAAAIJHPLWQ","head_branch":"DHIS2-20927-sequential-te-export","head_sha":"19b32d8c1deedea4cdefabe1da12d200466bae31","path":".github/workflows/run-tests.yml","run_number":56397,"run_attempt":1,"event":"pull_request","display_title":"perf: run tracked entity export fetches in series DHIS2-20927","status":"completed","conclusion":"success","workflow_id":10954,"check_suite_id":94699252006,"check_suite_node_id":"CS_kwDOA_1uaM8AAAAWDIPpJg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/runs/34971306841","html_url":"https://github.com/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/runs/34971306841","pull_requests":[{"id":4506015450,"number":25176,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/pulls/25176","head":{"ref":"DHIS2-20927-sequential-te-export","sha":"85d5472f97b75f4d717eec838b0436ea64f213db","repo":{"id":66940520,"name":"dhis2-core","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core"}},"base":{"ref":"master","sha":"5d2dbdef40e91c1c613fc50a8132158dd5683b7f","repo":{"id":66940520,"name":"dhis2-core","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core"}}}],"created_at":"2026-09-15T12:51:01Z","updated_at":"2026-09-15T13:00:43Z","run_started_at":"2026-09-15T12:51:01Z","jobs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/runs/34971306841/jobs","logs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/runs/34971306841/logs","check_suite_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/check-suites/94699252006","artifacts_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/runs/34971306841/artifacts","cancel_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/runs/34971306841/cancel","rerun_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/runs/34971306841/rerun","head_commit":{"message":"perf: run tracked entity export fetches in series DHIS2-20927\n\nTrackedEntityAggregate.find() fanned four fetches onto a JVM-wide unbounded\nnewCachedThreadPool and joined them. They now run in series on the request\nthread, and ThreadPoolManager is deleted.\n\nFour tasks were submitted regardless of fields, so a request needing one\nconnection still burned four threads. Same queries, same conditionals, same\nmerge; results verified identical (rows, order, content) across 7 fields\nshapes including fields=* and order=enrolledAt:desc.\n\nmax(branches) becomes sum(branches), so below saturation this is slower, and\nabove saturation holding one connection instead of four wins. Below saturation\n(CI compare, -Dprofile=load, three replicates) it costs 20ms p95 on \"Get first\npage of TEs\" and 9ms on \"Get TEs with enrollment status\", both fields=:all\nshapes where the enrollment branch dominates, while winning 7-9ms on lighter\nshapes from the removed per-branch MDC, SecurityContext and deadline\npropagation. At saturation (120 users, think time disabled) throughput goes\n113.3 -\u003e 117.8 rps with p95 2711 -\u003e 2592ms.\n\nOn this dataset the serial id query dominates the request, roughly 121ms\nagainst 20ms of branch work, so parallelising the branches could never save\nmuch here.\n\nTwo latent bugs surfaced, both masked by the fan-out:\n\nEnrollmentAggregate called obtainAuthentication and then clearAuthentication in\na finally. That is safe on a throwaway pool thread but wipes the caller's own\nSecurityContext when run inline, failing every later step of the request with\n\"No authentication found\".\n\nTrackerProgramService.getTrackerProgramStagesWithDataReadAccess read\nProgram#getProgramStages(), a lazy inverse collection that only resolved\nbecause each branch got a fresh Hibernate session. Run inline it joins the\ncaller's session, where an already-cached Program can return an empty\ncollection, which JdbcTrackerEventStore binds as ev.programstageid in (null),\nmatching no rows, so every event silently vanished from the export. Caught by\nTrackerDataSynchronizationServiceTest: a tracked entity whose child event\nfailed remotely was stamped as synchronized and would have been skipped on the\nnext sync. Fixed by querying the stages on the owning side.\n\nTest changes:\n\nAdded the shape the Android SDK sends on every online tracked entity search\n(NewTrackedEntityInstanceFields.asSearchFields: attributes and programOwners,\nno enrollments, pageSize 50). Every other /trackedEntities request in\nTrackerTest asks for enrollments, so that branch dominated and hid the other\nthree; this is the only covered shape where the four are comparable in cost.\n\nAdded -DdisablePauses so any profile can reach connection pool saturation. With\npause(1,3) a closed-injection user is idle around 98% of its cycle, so 120\nusers produce 2-3 in-flight requests and the pool peaks at 8 of 80.\n\nAdded unit tests for the gating and merge semantics, which had none, replacing\nWithRequestContextTest whose subject was removed.","author":{"name":"teleivo","email":"teleivo@users.noreply.github.com"},"id":"19b32d8c1deedea4cdefabe1da12d200466bae31","tree_id":"2a331d898e650337301c0fdaf227e0d8e069d16c","timestamp":"2026-09-15T12:50:45Z","committer":{"name":"teleivo","email":"teleivo@users.noreply.github.com"}},"workflow_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/workflows/10954","repository":{"id":66940520,"node_id":"MDEwOlJlcG9zaXRvcnk2Njk0MDUyMA==","owner":{"login":"dhis2","id":1089987,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjEwODk5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1089987?v=4","html_url":"https://github.com/dhis2","gravatar_id":"","type":"Organization","site_admin":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhis2","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhis2/events{/privacy}","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhis2/following{/other_user}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhis2/followers","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhis2/gists{/gist_id}","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhis2/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/use